# fixedbugs, defect 2318, 2026-11-07: beside the issue's shapes, a chain of
# bindings each made by a top-level function, `x1 = one(v: x0)`. A name is
# asked of the open bindings before the top level (`resolve/names.hero`'s
# `bare_name`), and `one`, which none binds, scanned every one of them at
# each call. The compiler's own instructions checking N such bindings at
# 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192: 2.29, 6.29 and 19.83 billion before, 1.42, 2.75
# and 5.43 after. This case, 2,048 and one binding that shadows the first,
# told naming its line: 1.88 billion before, 1.01 after.
function one(v: i64) -> i64
    return v + 1

function main()
    x0 = args().len()
    x1 = one(v: x0)
    x2 = one(v: x1)
    x3 = one(v: x2)
